# Cursor Rules for exporter

## Project Context

This is a Chrome extension that exports web pages to PDF entirely on-device. Zero network requests — enforced at build time.

## Critical Constraints

### Security Rules (MUST NOT violate)

These are ESLint errors, not warnings:

- NO `eval()` or `new Function()`
- NO `fetch()`, `XMLHttpRequest`, `WebSocket`, `EventSource`
- NO network calls of any kind in first-party code
- NO `console.log` (use `console.warn`, `console.error`, `console.debug`)

### Architecture Rules

- Content scripts (src/content/*) compile to IIFE — no imports allowed
- All chrome.runtime messages go through src/shared/messaging.ts
- Every onMessage handler MUST verify `sender.id === chrome.runtime.id`
- src/export/filename.ts is a security boundary — sanitizes attacker-controlled input
- No content_scripts in manifest — injection via chrome.scripting only

## Code Style

- TypeScript strict mode with `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`
- Use `import type { X }` for type-only imports
- Prefix unused variables with `_`
- No explicit `any` types

## File Patterns

- `src/background/` — Service worker, orchestrates all exports
- `src/content/` — Injected scripts (IIFE bundles, no imports)
- `src/export/` — PDF generation (CDP primary, canvas fallback)
- `src/shared/` — Types, messaging contract, utilities
- `vendor/` — Committed third-party code (no CDN)
- `scripts/` — Build tooling (Node environment, network allowed)
- `tests/` — Unit (Vitest) and e2e (Playwright)

## Commands

```bash
npm run build          # Build dist/
npm test               # Unit tests
npm run lint           # ESLint with security rules
npm run typecheck      # tsc --noEmit
npm run verify:no-remote  # Fail if dist/ has network paths
```

## When Adding Code

1. Check if it introduces network calls — that's a hard block
2. For content scripts: ensure no imports, must be self-contained
3. For new error codes: add to types.ts AND _locales/en/messages.json
4. For new messages: add to messaging.ts, add ResponseMap entry, verify sender.id

## Node Version

Node 22.13+ required. Use `nvm use` to activate.
